your profit per job drops,

867
00:27:48,875 --> 00:27:50,640
because you pay the worker,

868
00:27:50,640 --> 00:27:52,994
but the number of jobs can multiply.

869
00:27:53,174 --> 00:27:54,495
In this illustration,

870
00:27:54,495 --> 00:27:56,068
you earn more with crews,

871
00:27:56,068 --> 00:27:57,956
and your own time is freed for

872
00:27:57,956 --> 00:27:59,025
sales and growth.

873
00:27:59,376 --> 00:28:01,472
A simple signal that it's time to

874
00:28:01,472 --> 00:28:03,441
grow: you're turning away work,

875
00:28:03,441 --> 00:28:05,791
your prices are already fair or high,

876
00:28:05,791 --> 00:28:08,014
and you've had steady demand for at

877
00:28:08,014 --> 00:28:09,093
least six months.

878
00:28:09,273 --> 00:28:12,154
Before hiring, make sure your price leaves

879
00:28:12,154 --> 00:28:14,074
enough room to pay a worker,

880
00:28:14,074 --> 00:28:16,406
cover insurance and payroll taxes,

881
00:28:16,406 --> 00:28:18,600
and still make a profit on every

882
00:28:18,600 --> 00:28:18,875
job.

883
00:28:19,055 --> 00:28:21,462
A common mistake is hiring as soon

884
00:28:21,462 --> 00:28:22,666
as you feel busy,

885
00:28:22,666 --> 00:28:24,790
before the numbers support it.

886
00:28:24,970 --> 00:28:26,333
Run the math first:

887
00:28:26,333 --> 00:28:28,055
what you'll pay per job,

888
00:28:28,055 --> 00:28:30,709
what insurance and payroll taxes add,

889
00:28:30,709 --> 00:28:33,004
and how many jobs the new person

890
00:28:33,004 --> 00:28:35,157
needs to do each week to cover

891
00:28:35,157 --> 00:28:35,802
the cost.

892
00:28:35,982 --> 00:28:37,968
If the math works with a cushion,

893
00:28:37,968 --> 00:28:38,269
hire.

894
00:28:38,449 --> 00:28:40,539
If not, raise prices first.

895
00:28:40,889 --> 00:28:42,235
Taxes matter too.

896
00:28:42,415 --> 00:28:45,265
Side hustle income is generally taxable,

897
00:28:45,265 --> 00:28:47,971
and self employment tax applies to net

898
00:28:47,971 --> 00:28:50,322
earnings above a small threshold.

899
00:28:50,502 --> 00:28:51,628
As income grows,

900
00:28:51,628 --> 00:28:54,231
many owners form an LLC for liability

901
00:28:54,231 --> 00:28:57,327
protection and talk with an accountant about

902
00:28:57,327 --> 00:28:58,664
the best tax setup.

903
00:28:58,844 --> 00:29:01,692
Planning for taxes from the start avoids

904
00:29:01,692 --> 00:29:03,685
a painful surprise in April.

905
00:29:04,035 --> 00:29:05,242
Finally, value.

906
00:29:05,422 --> 00:29:07,130
A hustle that depends on you is

907
00:29:07,130 --> 00:29:08,452
worth little to a buyer.

908
00:29:08,632 --> 00:29:10,894
A business with recurring customers,

909
00:29:10,894 --> 00:29:13,720
trained staff and documented systems can sell

910
00:29:13,720 --> 00:29:15,981
for a multiple of its yearly profit.

911
00:29:16,161 --> 00:29:18,279
That's the real prize of making the

912
00:29:18,279 --> 00:29:20,155
jump: you're building an asset,

913
00:29:20,155 --> 00:29:21,305
not just an income.

914
00:29:21,655 --> 00:29:22,618
Second angle.

915
00:29:22,798 --> 00:29:23,901
The psychology.

916
00:29:24,081 --> 00:29:26,397
Why do so few side hustles become

917
00:29:26,397 --> 00:29:27,170
businesses?

918
00:29:27,520 --> 00:29:29,710
The first reason is the comfort of

919
00:29:29,710 --> 00:29:30,225
control.

920
00:29:30,405 --> 00:29:32,773
Doing everything yourself feels safe.

921
00:29:32,953 --> 00:29:34,613
You know the work is done right.

922
00:29:34,793 --> 00:29:36,474
Hiring means letting go,

923
00:29:36,474 --> 00:29:39,205
accepting mistakes and trusting others.

924
00:29:39,385 --> 00:29:40,799
But without letting go,

925
00:29:40,799 --> 00:29:42,090
growth is impossible.

926
00:29:42,441 --> 00:29:44,498
The second reason is fear of losing

927
00:29:44,498 --> 00:29:45,262
the paycheck.

928
00:29:45,442 --> 00:29:47,839
Many people stay stuck between a job

929
00:29:47,839 --> 00:29:49,370
and a hustle for years,

930
00:29:49,370 --> 00:29:51,434
too busy to grow and too scared

931
00:29:51,434 --> 00:29:51,967
to leap.

932
00:29:52,147 --> 00:29:54,529
The answer isn't to quit recklessly,

933
00:29:54,529 --> 00:29:56,382
but to set clear milestones:

934
00:29:56,382 --> 00:29:59,096
when the business earns a specific amount

935
00:29:59,096 --> 00:30:01,214
for a specific number of months,

936
00:30:01,214 --> 00:30:02,670
with savings in place,

937
00:30:02,670 --> 00:30:03,861
you make the move.

938
00:30:04,211 --> 00:30:06,208
The third reason is identity.

939
00:30:06,388 --> 00:30:09,303
Many hustlers see themselves as a cleaner,

940
00:30:09,303 --> 00:30:11,316
a photographer or a mechanic,

941
00:30:11,316 --> 00:30:12,982
not as a business owner.

942
00:30:13,162 --> 00:30:15,280
That identity keeps them working in the

943
00:30:15,280 --> 00:30:16,692
business instead of on it.

944
00:30:16,872 --> 00:30:18,849
Thinking of yourself as the owner,

945
00:30:18,849 --> 00:30:21,059
even when you're still doing the work,

946
00:30:21,059 --> 00:30:23,036
can change the decisions you make.

947
00:30:23,387 --> 00:30:24,176
The takeaway.

948
00:30:24,356 --> 00:30:26,596
The skills that start a hustle aren't

949
00:30:26,596 --> 00:30:28,896
the same skills that build a business.

950
00:30:29,076 --> 00:30:30,738
The jump requires letting go,

951
00:30:30,738 --> 00:30:33,030
planning the leap and seeing yourself as

952
00:30:33,030 --> 00:30:33,604
the owner.

953
00:30:33,954 --> 00:30:34,964
Third angle.

954
00:30:35,144 --> 00:30:35,829
The playbook.

955
00:30:36,009 --> 00:30:38,083
Here's how to go from first customer

956
00:30:38,083 --> 00:30:39,120
to first employee.

957
00:30:39,470 --> 00:30:40,259
Step one.

958
00:30:40,439 --> 00:30:42,808
Pick a hustle with recurring demand and

959
00:30:42,808 --> 00:30:44,023
a clear growth path,

960
00:30:44,023 --> 00:30:45,664
like the ones on this list.

961
00:30:45,844 --> 00:30:46,703
Step two.

962
00:30:46,883 --> 00:30:49,019
Start small and keep your job.

963
00:30:49,199 --> 00:30:51,444
Get your first ten paying customers and

964
00:30:51,444 --> 00:30:53,228
learn what they actually value.

965
00:30:53,578 --> 00:30:54,495
Step three.

966
00:30:54,675 --> 00:30:55,638
Make it official.

967
00:30:55,818 --> 00:30:57,391
Separate bank account,

968
00:30:57,391 --> 00:31:00,321
basic bookkeeping, any required licenses,

969
00:31:00,321 --> 00:31:01,322
and insurance.

970
00:31:01,502 --> 00:31:02,488
Step four.

971
00:31:02,668 --> 00:31:05,104
Raise prices until you're earning a healthy

972
00:31:05,104 --> 00:31:05,954
profit per job.

973
00:31:06,134 --> 00:31:07,098
Step five.

974
00:31:07,278 --> 00:31:09,178
Write down how you do the work,

975
00:31:09,178 --> 00:31:09,976
step by step,

976
00:31:09,976 --> 00:31:11,202
so you can teach it.

977
00:31:11,552 --> 00:31:12,666
Step six.

978
00:31:12,846 --> 00:31:14,266
Hire your first helper,

979
00:31:14,266 --> 00:31:15,253
maybe part time,

980
00:31:15,253 --> 00:31:17,722
and train them using your written steps.

981
00:31:17,902 --> 00:31:18,843
Step seven.

982
00:31:19,023 --> 00:31:20,897
Shift your time toward sales,

983
00:31:20,897 --> 00:31:23,934
recurring contracts and customer relationships.

984
00:31:24,114 --> 00:31:24,834
Step eight.

985
00:31:25,014 --> 00:31:28,012
When the business reliably replaces your income

986
00:31:28,012 --> 00:31:29,352
and you have savings,

987
00:31:29,352 --> 00:31:31,330
decide whether to go full time.

988
00:31:31,680 --> 00:31:33,130
Throughout all of it,

989
00:31:33,130 --> 00:31:35,961
keep investing for retirement and keep an

990
00:31:35,961 --> 00:31:36,997
emergency fund.

991
00:31:37,177 --> 00:31:39,126
A growing business is exciting,

992
00:31:39,126 --> 00:31:42,333
but your personal financial foundation should never

993
00:31:42,333 --> 00:31:43,528
depend on it alone.

994
00:31:43,878 --> 00:31:44,702
Question one.

995
00:31:44,882 --> 00:31:46,421
How much money do I need to

996
00:31:46,421 --> 00:31:46,763
start?

997
00:31:46,943 --> 00:31:48,823
Many of these hustles start with a

998
00:31:48,823 --> 00:31:50,868
few hundred to a few thousand dollars

999
00:31:50,868 --> 00:31:51,587
in equipment.

1000
00:31:51,767 --> 00:31:53,313
Start with the minimum,

1001
00:31:53,313 --> 00:31:54,994
and upgrade with profits.

1002
00:31:55,174 --> 00:31:55,929
Question two.

1003
00:31:56,109 --> 00:31:57,433
Do I need an LLC?

1004
00:31:57,613 --> 00:31:59,721
Not always at the very start,

1005
00:31:59,721 --> 00:32:01,758
but as income and risk grow,

1006
00:32:01,758 --> 00:32:04,448
an LLC and insurance can protect your

1007
00:32:04,448 --> 00:32:05,612
personal assets.

1008
00:32:05,792 --> 00:32:07,359
Ask a local professional.

1009
00:32:07,709 --> 00:32:08,754
Question three.

1010
00:32:08,934 --> 00:32:11,256
How do I find my first customers?

1011
00:32:11,436 --> 00:32:14,493
Friends, neighbors, local social media groups,

1012
00:32:14,493 --> 00:32:18,017
online listings and simply asking satisfied customers

1013
00:32:18,017 --> 00:32:18,947
for referrals.

1014
00:32:19,127 --> 00:32:20,068
Question four.

1015
00:32:20,248 --> 00:32:22,885
Which hustle grows into the most valuable

1016
00:32:22,885 --> 00:32:23,464
business?

1017
00:32:23,644 --> 00:32:25,495
Those with recurring revenue,

1018
00:32:25,495 --> 00:32:27,858
like bookkeeping, cleaning contracts,

1019
00:32:27,858 --> 00:32:30,157
lawn care routes and vending routes,

1020
00:32:30,157 --> 00:32:32,264
tend to be the most valuable when

1021
00:32:32,264 --> 00:32:32,839
you sell.

1022
00:32:33,189 --> 00:32:34,234
Question five.

1023
00:32:34,414 --> 00:32:36,331
Should I use gig apps or find

1024
00:32:36,331 --> 00:32:37,455
my own customers?

1025
00:32:37,635 --> 00:32:39,235
Apps can be a great way to

1026
00:32:39,235 --> 00:32:40,465
get started quickly,

1027
00:32:40,465 --> 00:32:42,372
but they take a cut and control

1028
00:32:42,372 --> 00:32:43,417
the relationship.

1029
00:32:43,597 --> 00:32:45,549
The goal is to move customers to

1030
00:32:45,549 --> 00:32:47,257
your own business over time,

1031
00:32:47,257 --> 00:32:49,271
where you set the prices and keep

1032
00:32:49,271 --> 00:32:50,308
the relationship.

1033
00:32:50,488 --> 00:32:51,556
Question six.

1034
00:32:51,736 --> 00:32:53,598
How many hours a week does it

1035
00:32:53,598 --> 00:32:53,919
take?

1036
00:32:54,099 --> 00:32:56,496
Many people start with ten to fifteen

1037
00:32:56,496 --> 00:32:58,505
hours on evenings and weekends,

1038
00:32:58,505 --> 00:33:00,449
then increase as demand grows.

1039
00:33:00,799 --> 00:33:01,728
Question seven.

1040
00:33:01,908 --> 00:33:02,871
What if I fail?

1041
00:33:03,051 --> 00:33:05,903
Most side hustles cost little to start,

1042
00:33:05,903 --> 00:33:08,317
so the downside is usually small:

1043
00:33:08,317 --> 00:33:10,145
some money and some time.

1044
00:33:10,325 --> 00:33:12,730
And even a failed hustle teaches sales,

1045
00:33:12,730 --> 00:33:14,519
pricing and customer service,

1046
00:33:14,519 --> 00:33:16,800
skills that make the next attempt far

1047
00:33:16,800 --> 00:33:18,034
more likely to work.

1048
00:33:18,384 --> 00:33:19,742
Let's recap the twenty.

1049
00:33:19,922 --> 00:33:21,013
Pressure washing.

1050
00:33:21,193 --> 00:33:22,076
Lawn care.

1051
00:33:22,256 --> 00:33:23,289
House cleaning.

1052
00:33:23,469 --> 00:33:24,317
Bookkeeping.

1053
00:33:24,497 --> 00:33:25,704
Mobile detailing.

1054
00:33:25,884 --> 00:33:26,383
Vending.

1055
00:33:26,563 --> 00:33:27,968
Handyman services.

1056
00:33:28,148 --> 00:33:29,297
Junk removal.

1057
00:33:29,477 --> 00:33:30,174
Pet care.

1058
00:33:30,354 --> 00:33:30,969
Tutoring.

1059
00:33:31,149 --> 00:33:31,858
Reselling.

1060
00:33:32,038 --> 00:33:33,500
Social media management.

1061
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:34,586
Photography.

1062
00:33:34,766 --> 00:33:35,985
Home kitchen food.

1063
00:33:36,165 --> 00:33:37,256
Event rentals.

1064
00:33:37,436 --> 00:33:38,574
Mobile mechanic.

1065
00:33:38,754 --> 00:33:39,579
Moving help.

1066
00:33:39,759 --> 00:33:41,117
Airbnb co hosting.

1067
00:33:41,297 --> 00:33:43,027
Window and gutter cleaning.

1068
00:33:43,207 --> 00:33:44,681
And digital products.

1069
00:33:45,031 --> 00:33:45,959
And the path.

1070
00:33:46,139 --> 00:33:48,168
Do everything, fill your schedule,

1071
00:33:48,168 --> 00:33:49,540
hire your first helper,

1072
00:33:49,540 --> 00:33:51,747
build systems, then become the owner.

1073
00:33:51,927 --> 00:33:53,021
Price for profit,

1074
00:33:53,021 --> 00:33:54,565
chase recurring revenue,

1075
00:33:54,565 --> 00:33:57,075
keep your job until the business proves

1076
00:33:57,075 --> 00:33:59,971
itself, and protect your foundation the whole

1077
00:33:59,971 --> 00:34:00,228
way.

1078
00:34:00,578 --> 00:34:03,715
Remember, every large service company you see

1079
00:34:03,715 --> 00:34:07,131
today, the cleaning company with fifty employees,

1080
00:34:07,131 --> 00:34:09,641
the landscaping firm with a fleet of

1081
00:34:09,641 --> 00:34:12,569
trucks, the agency with dozens of clients,

1082
00:34:12,569 --> 00:34:15,427
started with one person and one customer.

1083
00:34:15,607 --> 00:34:18,011
The difference between them and the millions

1084
00:34:18,011 --> 00:34:20,251
of hustles that stayed small wasn't luck.

1085
00:34:20,431 --> 00:34:21,596
It was a decision,

1086
00:34:21,596 --> 00:34:22,826
made at some point,

1087
00:34:22,826 --> 00:34:25,026
to stop being the worker and start

1088
00:34:25,026 --> 00:34:26,062
being the owner.

1089
00:34:26,242 --> 00:34:28,312
That decision is available to you too,

1090
00:34:28,312 --> 00:34:30,328
whenever your hustle is ready for it.

1091
00:34:30,679 --> 00:34:32,762
Pick one hustle from this list that

1092
00:34:32,762 --> 00:34:33,953
matches your skills.

1093
00:34:34,133 --> 00:34:36,652
This week, get your first paying customer,

1094
00:34:36,652 --> 00:34:38,092
even if it's a neighbor.

1095
00:34:38,272 --> 00:34:40,181
Then start writing down how you do

1096
00:34:40,181 --> 00:34:40,687
the work.

1097
00:34:40,867 --> 00:34:42,676
That list is the first page of

1098
00:34:42,676 --> 00:34:43,943
your future business.

1099
00:34:44,123 --> 00:34:45,255
Then keep going:

1100
00:34:45,255 --> 00:34:47,165
ten customers, then twenty,

1101
00:34:47,165 --> 00:34:49,499
then the day you realize you have

1102
00:34:49,499 --> 00:34:50,985
more work than hours.

1103
00:34:51,165 --> 00:34:52,212
When that day comes,

1104
00:34:52,212 --> 00:34:53,417
don't just work harder.

1105
00:34:53,597 --> 00:34:55,687
Hire, train and build.

1106
00:34:55,867 --> 00:34:58,003
That's the moment a side hustle starts

1107
00:34:58,003 --> 00:34:59,071
becoming a company.

1108
00:34:59,251 --> 00:35:00,884
And if you start one of these,

1109
00:35:00,884 --> 00:35:02,681
tell me in the comments which one

1110
00:35:02,681 --> 00:35:03,280
you picked.

1111
00:35:03,460 --> 00:35:04,120
I read them,

1112
00:35:04,120 --> 00:35:06,209
and your story might help someone else

1113
00:35:06,209 --> 00:35:07,419
take their first step.

1114
00:35:07,599 --> 00:35:08,818
I'm Ryan Rover.

1115
00:35:08,998 --> 00:35:10,698
Start small, think big,

1116
00:35:10,698 --> 00:35:12,769
and I'll see you in the next

1117
00:35:12,769 --> 00:35:13,212
video.
